    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test class, 0 failures).\n\n## What I changed\n\nThe `initials` field is exposed on the JSON representation of an `Owner`, which is an OpenAPI-generated DTO (`OwnerDto`) populated by a MapStruct mapper. Two edits:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`).\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a mapping that computes it:\n   ```java\n   @Mapping(target = \"initials\",\n       expression = \"java(Character.toUpperCase(owner.getFirstName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\" + Character.toUpperCase(owner.getLastName().charAt(0)) + \\\".\\\")\")\n   ```\n\nThis upper-cases the first letters of `firstName` and `lastName` and joins them dot-separated with a trailing dot, so `\"john\"` / `\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`, matching the spec and the acceptance test (`$.initials == \"J.S.\"`).",
